<ArticleLayout title="Privacy Policy" headings={headings} notice="Cloud is not yet available. The Cloud-specific sections below describe the planned service; the open-source CLI is governed by its MIT license.">
<h1>Privacy Policy</h1><p>Last updated <time datetime="2026-09-01">2026-09-01</time> · Applies to oauthlint.dev and OAuthLint Cloud</p><p>We collect as little as we can. The CLI runs on your machine and sends nothing unless you upload findings.</p><h2 id="what-we-collect">What we collect</h2><ul><li><strong>Account</strong>: name, email, and the organisation you belong to.</li><li><strong>Findings</strong>: rule, file path, line and, only if you turn it on, the surrounding code.</li><li><strong>Usage</strong>: anonymous counts of which rules fire. You can turn this off.</li><li><strong>Billing</strong>: handled by Stripe. We never see your full card number.</li></ul><h2 id="what-we-do-not-collect">What we do not collect</h2><p>Your source code, unless you choose to send snippets. Repository contents beyond what a scan reads. Anything from the self-hosted app.</p><h2 id="where-data-lives">Where data lives</h2><p>OAuthLint Cloud runs in the EU (Frankfurt). Sub-processors are listed below, and we notify you 30 days before adding one.</p><h2 id="sub-processors">Sub-processors</h2><ul><li>Stripe — payments</li><li>Postmark — transactional email</li><li>Cloudflare — network and DNS</li><li>AWS eu-central-1 — hosting and storage</li></ul><h2 id="your-rights">Your rights</h2><p>You can access, correct, export or delete your data from Settings, or by writing to <a href="mailto:privacy@auspeo.dev">privacy@auspeo.dev</a>. You can also complain to your data protection authority.</p><h2 id="cookies">Cookies</h2><p>We use only the cookies needed to keep you signed in. No advertising or cross-site tracking.</p>
</ArticleLayout>
